On Monday 19 April 2004 06:14, Evgeni Sklyanin wrote:
> coi rod

mi'enai rod miku'i dafyfra

> jbofi'e does not recognize lujvo {kadybunre} whereas it does permit
> {kandybunre} and {labybunre}. What is wrong? --- {kad} as I
> understand it, is as legitimate rafsi from {kandi} as {lab} from
> {blabi}.

The word is {kadbunre}. "db" can occur in the middle of a brivla, but not at 
the beginning. "bb" cannot occur anywhere in a word, so {labbunre} is an 
invalid form. {kandybunre} requires the 'y' because {kand} is a long rafsi.

